  "notes": [
    "Unlike Dutch stroopwafels (which are thick, chewy, and filled with caramel), traditional Italian pizzelle are single-layer, thin wafer cookies pressed on a patterned iron to deliver a light, delicate snap.",
    "Pairs exceptionally well with hot espresso, dark-roast pour-overs, robust black teas, or earthy matcha, which naturally balance the cocoa sweetness.",
    "Can be served as a quick accompaniment to an affogato, crushed over ice cream and pudding, or layered with hazelnut spread or gelato into a sandwich cookie.",
    "Because thin waffle cookies easily absorb ambient humidity and lose their crunch, store any uneaten cookies in an airtight container at room temperature to preserve their crisp texture."
